# Admin Frontend Standards

## Angular Material Components

Always use Angular Material (`@angular/material`) components. Never use raw HTML equivalents for UI elements.

```html
<!-- BAD -->
<button>Save</button>
<input type="text" />
<table>...</table>

<!-- GOOD -->
<button mat-raised-button>Save</button>
<mat-form-field><input matInput /></mat-form-field>
<mat-table [dataSource]="dataSource">...</mat-table>
```

## Material Color Tokens — No Hardcoded Colors

Always use Material 3 CSS color tokens via `var(--mat-*)` or `var(--mdc-*)`. Never hardcode hex, RGB, HSL, or named colors in `.scss` files or inline styles.

```scss
// BAD
color: #1976d2;
background: rgb(255, 255, 255);
border-color: blue;

// GOOD
color: var(--mat-primary-color);
background: var(--mat-app-background-color);
border-color: var(--mat-divider-color);
```

## Material Theme Defaults

Do not override Material component internal styles with custom colors. Let the configured theme palette control color, typography, and elevation. Only customize via the Angular Material theme definition (e.g. `mat.define-theme`), never by targeting internal MDC classes directly.

## Shared Interfaces

Any interface used by both `eatfit247-admin` and `server_1` must be defined in `shared-library/src/` and imported via the `@eatfit247-shared-lib` path alias.

```typescript
// BAD — duplicating an interface that server also uses
interface IProgram { id: number; name: string; }

// GOOD
import { IProgram } from '@eatfit247-shared-lib';
```

Frontend-only interfaces (not consumed by the server) may be defined within the admin app.

## No `any` Keyword

Never use `any` in TypeScript. Define a typed interface or use a specific union/generic instead.

```typescript
// BAD
getData(): any { ... }
const result: any = response;

// GOOD
getData(): IApiResponse<IProgram[]> { ... }
const result: IApiResponse<IProgram[]> = response;
```
